# BuildList — Netlify redirects
# A product of Sharplink Ventures (U) Limited
# Docs: https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/

# ── Friendly paths → the matching in-app route ───────
# The site is a single HTML file that routes on the hash, so a clean
# path like /directory is redirected to /#/directory. This is what
# makes printed URLs and business-card links work.
/directory    /browse/       301
/tenders      /#/tenders     301
/jobs         /#/jobs        301
/news         /#/news        301
/prices       /#/news        301
/advertise    /#/advertise   301
/submit       /#/submit      301
/add-listing  /#/submit      301
/about        /#/about       301
/contact      /#/about       301
/privacy      /#/privacy     301
/privacy-policy /#/privacy   301
/terms        /#/terms       301
/terms-of-service /#/terms   301

# ── Static pages (Stage 5) ───────────────────────────
# /firms/*, /browse/*, /tenders/*, /news/* are REAL generated HTML
# files with their own titles and structured data. Netlify serves
# them directly — do not redirect them into the hash router or the
# whole point of Stage 5 is lost.

